:: Dragon Quest {"position":"1025,1400","size":"100,100"}
Your journey takes you into the mountains beyond the northern border.

The path becomes increasingly difficult as you approach the ruins of the Fallen Kingdom.

Broken towers stretch toward the sky, and enormous statues lie buried beneath the earth.

Your crystal pendant begins to vibrate.

A deep voice echoes throughout the ruins.

Dragon: "Who dares enter the remains of a kingdom long forgotten?"

A massive dragon emerges from the ruins.

Its scales shimmer with silver and violet, and its eyes glow like burning embers.

Dragon: "Another treasure hunter? Or perhaps another fool seeking the secrets of the past?"
{
(if: $firstGuardian is "Leviathan")[
    Dragon: "I can sense the ocean's blessing upon you."

    Dragon: "The sea has always been too trusting of outsiders."
]
(else-if: $firstGuardian is "Phoenix")[
    Dragon: "The Phoenix has shared its knowledge with you?"

    Dragon: "Then perhaps you have already learned more than most mortals ever will."
]
(else-if: $firstGuardian is "Warden")[
    Dragon: "The crystals recognize you."

    Dragon: "That power should have remained buried with this kingdom."
]
}
Dragon: "Tell me, traveler. Why have you come?"

[[I seek the truth about the Great Sundering->DragonTrial]]


:: DragonMemory {"position":"1025,1650","size":"100,100"}
You search the abandoned ruins and recover the three fragments.

As you place them together, the royal seal begins to glow.

A strange vision appears before you.

You see the ancient kingdom as it once existed.

Magnificent towers stretch across the landscape.

Celestial symbols illuminate the night sky.

And standing before an enormous throne is a mysterious figure surrounded by four lights.

The vision suddenly disappears.

The dragon approaches.

Dragon: "So you have seen it."

Dragon: "The kingdom did not fall because of a simple disaster."

Dragon: "Someone attempted to change the balance of the realms."

Dragon: "The guardians were forced to intervene."

Dragon: "But even their combined power was not enough."

The dragon lowers its head.

Dragon: "There was another presence. A celestial power unlike anything the kingdom had ever witnessed."

Dragon: "I cannot tell you whether that power saved our world or brought about its destruction."

Dragon: "The truth was lost with the kingdom."

The dragon gives you a fragment of its ancient scale.

Dragon: "Take this. You have earned it."
{
(set: $dragonDone to true)

(if: $firstGuardian is "none")[
    (set: $firstGuardian to "Dragon")

    The pendant glows with a violet light.

    A strange warmth spreads through the ancient crystal.
]
}
[[Return to the guardian map->Quest Hub]]


:: DragonTrial {"position":"925,1525","size":"100,100"}
Dragon: "The Great Sundering..."

The dragon lets out a low growl.

Dragon: "A catastrophe that should never have occurred."

Dragon: "You wish to understand what happened to this kingdom?"

Dragon: "Then prove that you are worthy of knowing."

The dragon points toward three ancient structures surrounding the ruined castle.

Dragon: "Within these ruins are three fragments of the royal seal."

Dragon: "Recover them and bring them to the throne room."

Dragon: "But understand this. The past is not always something that should be uncovered."

[[Accept the Dragon's trial->DragonMemory]]


:: End {"position":"1250,800","size":"100,100"}
The archivist watches as you begin gathering your belongings.

Royal Archivist: "Leaving already?"

{(if: $learnedHistory and $learnedGuardians
and $learnedEvents)[

    Royal Archivist: "Well, you've certainly learned quite a bit today."

	Royal Archivist: "I hope the things I've shared with you have given you a better understanding of our world."

]
(else:)[

    Royal Archivist: "There is still much about this world that remains undiscovered."

    Royal Archivist: "Perhaps you'll find yourself curious enough to return."

]

(if: $learnedGirl)[

    Royal Archivist: "And do keep an eye on the ocean, traveler."

    Royal Archivist: "If the stories are true, the Princess may not remain a mystery forever."

]}

The archivist gives you a small nod.

Royal Archivist: "Until we meet again. May the tides guide your journey."

You leave the archive and step back into the quiet village.

THE END

[[Start Over->THE FORGOTTEN TIDES]]



