:: THE FORGOTTEN TIDES {"position":"900,550","size":"100,100"}
Royal Archivist: "Ah a visitor. It's been quite some time since we've had anyone travel this far into the kingdom."

Royal Archivist: "You've probably noticed the strange happenings around the village."

Royal Archivist: "The ocean has not been behaving as it should."

Royal Archivist: "For centuries, these lands have been protected by ancient guardians. Their stories have been passed down through generations, though most people consider them nothing more than fairy tales."

Royal Archivist: "But I fear those stories may be more imporant than we once believed."

Royal Archivist: "Perhaps you can help me uncover something I've spent years trying to understand."

[[Royal Archivist: What would you like to know? ->Story Hub]]

[[Nevermind... ->End]]


:: The Fallen Kingdom {"position":"750,800","size":"100,100"}
The archivist's expression becomes more
serious.

He reaches beneath his desk and pulls out a dusty map.

Royal Archivist: "The Fallen Kingdom..."

Royal Archivist: "A rather unfortunate chapter in our world's history."

He spreads the map across the desk.

Royal Archivist: "Before the Great Sundering, our world was not divided into the separate territories we know today."

Royal Archivist: "There was once a great central kingdom that connected all the realms."

Royal Archivist: "It was a place where different civilizations lived together, where magic was studied, and where the ancient guardians were said to reside."

He points toward the center of the map.

Royal Archivist: "At the heart of it stood a magnificent kingdom. Its people possessed knowledge far beyond anything we understand today."

Royal Archivist: "They studied the stars, the elements, and even the very foundations of magic itself."

He pauses.

Royal Archivist: "Then came the Great Sundering."

Royal Archivist: "No one knows exactly what happened. Some records describe a catastrophic event that tore the world apart."

Royal Archivist: "Others speak of an enormous surge of magical energy that shattered the kingdom and scattered its territories across the world."

Royal Archivist: "Entire cities disappeared. Ancient structures crumbled. The paths connecting the realms were lost."

Royal Archivist: "And strangely enough, many of the records describing the event were destroyed or deliberately hidden."

He rolls the map back up.

Royal Archivist: "Some historians believe the four ancient guardians were involved."

Royal Archivist: "But whether they caused the Sundering or tried to prevent it..."

Royal Archivist: "That is something I have yet to discover."
{
(set: $learnedHistory to true)
}
[[Return to the conversation.->Story Hub]]


:: The Four Guardians {"position":"875,800","size":"100,100"}
The archivist's eyes light up as you mention the ancient guardians.

Royal Archivist: "Ah! Now that is a subject I could discuss for hours."

He walks over to a nearby bookshelf and retrieves an enormous illustrated manuscript.

Royal Archivist: "According to the oldest records, four extraordinary creatures once watched over our world."

He opens the manuscript.

Royal Archivist: "Each guardian was connected to a different realm, and each possessed powers unlike anything ordinary beings could comprehend."

He turns to the first illustration.

Royal Archivist: "The first was the Leviathan, guardian of the oceans."

Royal Archivist: "An enormous creature said to dwell beneath the deepest waters."

Royal Archivist: "Sailors feared its enormous silhouette, but ancient records describe it as a protector rather than a monster."

He turns another page.

Royal Archivist: "The second was the Ancient Dragon, guardian of the Fallen Kingdom."

Royal Archivist: "A creature of immense strength and wisdom, said to protect the remains of the civilization that existed before the Great Sundering."

He turns another page.

Royal Archivist: "The third was the Celestial Phoenix, guardian of the Shattered Skies."

Royal Archivist: "Its feathers were said to shine like the stars themselves. Some believed it possessed the ability to preserve memories and restore what was lost."

Finally, he turns to the last illustration.

Royal Archivist: "And the fourth..."

Royal Archivist: "The Crystal Warden, guardian of the Forgotten Realm."

Royal Archivist: "A mysterious being connected to the ancient crystal network that once maintained the balance of magic throughout the world."

He closes the manuscript.

Royal Archivist: "Each guardian served a purpose. Together, they maintained the balance between the realms."

Royal Archivist: "But after the Great Sundering, their stories slowly disappeared."

Royal Archivist: "Some believe they perished. Others believe they retreated into their respective territories."

Royal Archivist: "Personally, I believe they are still out there."

He looks toward the window.

Royal Archivist: "And if the recent disturbances are anything to go by, perhaps they are beginning to awaken."
{
(set: $learnedGuardians to true)
}
[[Return to the conversation.->Story Hub]]


:: The Kingdom of Tides {"position":"625,800","size":"100,100"}
The archivist walks toward a large window overlooking the distant ocean.

Royal Archivist: "The Kingdom of Tides..."

Royal Archivist: "A beautiful place, isn't it? At least, it was once considered the jewel of the old world."

He gestures toward the ocean.

Royal Archivist: "Long before our village existed, these waters were home to an enormous civilization."

Royal Archivist: "Its people built magnificent cities along the coastlines and even beneath the ocean itself."

Royal Archivist: "They believed the sea was more than just a source of life. They believed it was a living force, one connected to the stars and the celestial realm."

He takes a small crystal from his desk.

Royal Archivist: "These crystals were once used throughout the kingdom. They carried magical energy and helped maintain the kingdom's defenses."

Royal Archivist: "Some say they were gifts from the celestial beings who watched over the world."

Royal Archivist: "Others believe they were created by the ancient guardians themselves."

He places the crystal back on the desk.

Royal Archivist: "Unfortunately, much of that knowledge was lost during the Great Sundering."

Royal Archivist: "The ocean kingdom was among the few territories that managed to survive the catastrophe, though not without losing much of its history."

Royal Archivist: "Many of our oldest structures are now buried beneath the waves."

Royal Archivist: "There are even rumors of an entire palace hidden somewhere beneath the ocean floor."

Royal Archivist: "I sometimes wonder what secrets it might still contain."

He returns to his desk.

Royal Archivist: "Perhaps one day, someone will uncover what was lost."

[[Return to the conversation.->Story Hub]]


:: The Mysterious Girl {"position":"500,800","size":"100,100"}
The archivist pauses for a moment before reaching for an old book resting on his desk.

Royal Archivist: "Ah, yes. The girl."

Royal Archivist: "I had a feeling you might ask about her. It seems the stories have begun spreading beyond the village."

He opens the book, revealing an illustration of a mysterious winged figure surrounded by waves and stars.

Royal Archivist: "There have been countless accounts of a strange girl appearing along the coastline."

Royal Archivist: "Some fishermen claim to have seen her standing upon the surface of the ocean, as though the water itself were carrying her."

Royal Archivist: "Others speak of enormous wings, glowing like the colors of the deepest ocean, and a halo that shines like the stars above."

He turns another page.

Royal Archivist: "The oldest records refer to her as the Princess of the Oceans."

Royal Archivist: "A rather unusual title, don't you think? Especially considering that no one seems to know where she came from."

Royal Archivist: "Some believe she is a celestial being sent to protect our world. Others believe she is an ancient sea spirit."

Royal Archivist: "Personally, I find the latter rather difficult to believe. Though, I suppose I have seen stranger things in these archives."

He closes the book.

Royal Archivist: "Whatever she may be, there is one thing the stories seem to agree on."

Royal Archivist: "Whenever the ocean is in danger, she is never far away."

Royal Archivist: "Perhaps she is nothing more than a legend. But I have a feeling there is some truth behind these tales."
{(set: $learnedGirl to true)}
[[Return to the conversation.->Story Hub]]


:: The Royal Request {"position":"1125,800","size":"100,100"}
{(if: $learnedHistory and $learnedGuardians)[
    The archivist watches you for a moment, seemingly lost in thought.
    
    Royal Archivist: "I see you've been paying attention to the stories I've shared."
    
    He glances toward the old manuscript resting on his desk.
    
    Royal Archivist: "There is something I've been meaning to discuss with you."
    
    Royal Archivist: "You see, the history of the Fallen Kingdom and the four guardians are far more connected than most people realize."
    
