:: The Strange Occurrences {"position":"1000,800","size":"100,100"}
The archivist sighs and looks toward the window.

Royal Archivist: "I'm afraid this is the reason I've been spending so much time in these archives lately."

Royal Archivist: "Something is happening throughout the kingdom."

He pulls out a collection of letters and reports.

Royal Archivist: "It started a few months ago. At first, the villagers thought the ocean was simply experiencing unusual weather."

Royal Archivist: "But then the reports began to grow stranger."

He hands you the first report.

Royal Archivist: "Fishermen have reported seeing enormous shadows moving beneath the water."

Royal Archivist: "Some claim they heard a beautiful melody coming from the ocean during the night."

He hands you another report.

Royal Archivist: "Travelers returning from the northern mountains have spoken of strange lights appearing above the ruins of the Fallen Kingdom."

Royal Archivist: "Others have reported hearing what sounds like distant roaring."

He places another letter on the desk.

Royal Archivist: "And then there is the matter of the old observatory."

Royal Archivist: "It has been abandoned for centuries, yet recently, its celestial mechanisms have begun activating on their own."

He pauses before continuing.

Royal Archivist: "Perhaps the strangest report comes from the Forgotten Realm."

Royal Archivist: "Several travelers claim that the ancient crystals scattered throughout the region have started glowing again."

Royal Archivist: "All four territories. All at once."

He gathers the reports.

Royal Archivist: "Do you see the connection?"

Royal Archivist: "The ocean, the mountains, the skies, and the forgotten lands..."

Royal Archivist: "The four guardians."

Royal Archivist: "I cannot say for certain what is happening, but I fear something has disturbed the balance that once held this world together."

He lowers his voice.

Royal Archivist: "And if my suspicions are correct, the Princess of the Oceans may know more than anyone."
{
(set: $learnedEvents to true)
}
[[Return to the conversation.->Story Hub]]


:: Warden Quest {"position":"1275,1400","size":"100,100"}
Your final destination lies beyond the shattered territories.

The Forgotten Realm is strangely quiet.

Trees covered in glowing crystals surround an abandoned civilization.

The ground is scattered with broken fragments of ancient magical structures.

Your pendant begins to glow.

A faint voice echoes through the forest.

Unknown Voice: "The light..."

Unknown Voice: "It has been so long..."

You follow the sound toward a clearing.

At its center rests a magnificent creature resembling a stag.

Its body is covered in crystalline structures, though many have lost their glow.

Crystal Warden: "Who has come to disturb this forgotten place?"
{
(if: $firstGuardian is "Leviathan")[
    Crystal Warden: "The ocean has shared its blessing with you."

    Crystal Warden: "The ancient currents are beginning to move."
]
(else-if: $firstGuardian is "Dragon")[
    Crystal Warden: "The Fallen Kingdom..."

    Crystal Warden: "So the old memories are finally being uncovered."
]
(else-if: $firstGuardian is "Phoenix")[
    Crystal Warden: "The stars have revealed their memories to you."

    Crystal Warden: "Then perhaps there is still hope."
]
}
Crystal Warden: "The crystals have lost their light."

Crystal Warden: "Without them, this realm cannot awaken."

[[I want to help restore this place->WardenRestoration]]


:: WardenRestoration {"position":"1425,1525","size":"100,100"}
Crystal Warden: "Then listen carefully."

Crystal Warden: "Throughout this realm are three ancient crystal pillars."

Crystal Warden: "They once connected the four territories through a network of magical energy."

Crystal Warden: "But when the world was shattered, their power was lost."

Crystal Warden: "Find the missing crystal fragments and return them to the pillars."

Crystal Warden: "Only then can the Forgotten Realm awaken again."

You explore the abandoned structures and recover the missing fragments.

One by one, you restore the ancient pillars.

A brilliant wave of light travels throughout the realm.

The trees begin to glow.

The crystals scattered throughout the ruins illuminate the forest.

The Crystal Warden slowly rises.

Crystal Warden: "The light..."

Crystal Warden: "I remember now."

The creature approaches you.

Crystal Warden: "The world was once held together by a single source of celestial magic."

Crystal Warden: "The guardians were created to maintain its balance."

Crystal Warden: "But the source of that magic was never the guardians themselves."

Crystal Warden: "It belonged to
the celestial princess."

The Warden looks toward your pendant.

Crystal Warden: "She is the heart that connects the four realms."

Crystal Warden: "Without her, the world will never truly return to what it once was."

The Warden gives you a glowing crystal fragment.

Crystal Warden: "Take this."

Crystal Warden: "May it guide you toward the one who watches over the oceans."
{
